    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **262 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `selfLink` field is a derived, read-only property on the owner resource, so I implemented it the same way the other derived fields (`displayName`, `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, \u2026) are done in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` string property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces the getter/setter on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(formatSelfLink(owner))\")` and a `formatSelfLink` default method that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (and `null` when the id isn't assigned, so it's omitted rather than emitting `/api/owners/null`).\n\nBecause both the create (`addOwner`) and read (`getOwner`) paths run the owner through `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `selfLink = \"/api/owners/{id}\"`, satisfying the acceptance test.",
